CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260714T171119Z
DESCRIPTION:Round out your Labor Day weekend with one of Duke's most antic
 ipated musical traditions! The Duke Symphony Orchestra launches its 2026-
 27 season with a lively concert in the iconic Baldwin Auditorium.\n\nEnjo
 y an exhilarating evening of musical favorites by American composers as t
 he orchestra fills Baldwin with the energy and excitement of a new season
 . Festive\, family-friendly\, and full of spirit\, this annual celebratio
 n brings the Duke and Durham communities together through the joy of live
  music.\n\nBring your friends and family and join us as we kick off an ex
 citing new season of performances.\n\nThis event is part of "We the Peopl
 e\," a Duke and Durham collaboration marking the 250th anniversary of the
  signing of the Declaration of Independence through public events that ex
 amine the nation's evolving identity. Drawing from the opening words of t
 he Constitution\, the project invites us to consider who "the people" hav
 e been and who we aspire to be within the ongoing story of the United Sta
 tes.\n\nThis event is free and open to the public. All are welcome.
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260904T161142Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260906T180000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T161142Z
