CATEGORIES:Research
CATEGORIES:Main
CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a0052c8-9f41fc86-019f-42316fef-00000560:Dalton\, S
 tacy
X-BEDEWORK-COST:Free: registration requested
CREATED:20260813T182704Z
DESCRIPTION:In this talk\, Savchyna will share findings from the STRONG st
 udy (Stress\, Trauma\, Resilience Of New Generations)\, in which her team
  followed 141 Ukrainian refugee women - mothers and grandmothers who arri
 ved in Kraków after February 2022 - measuring hair cortisol concentration
  as a biomarker of HPA (hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal) axis activity alo
 ngside self-reported perceived stress and psychological resilience. \n\nW
 omen who escaped from frontline towns in Ukraine had 18% higher hair cort
 isol than those from non-frontline regions\, yet the two groups did not d
 iffer in perceived stress\; and the size of the cortisol gap depended on 
 resilience: it was largest among women with low resilience and disappeare
 d at high resilience. Savchnya will use this as a starting point to talk 
 about what biomarkers can add to refugee health research\, and future dir
 ections of her work\, including other biomarkers\, health systems perspec
 tive on refugees from Ukraine in Poland\, and a One Health project in pre
 paration. \n\nThe talk will allow time for discussion and feedback about 
 how stress is measured in war-affected families\, and what that might mea
 n for the how war-affected families are supported. \n\nMariia Savchyna co
 mpleted her medical education in Kyiv\, Ukraine (Bogomolets National Medi
 cal University) before moving to Poland for her PhD in Health Sciences at
  Jagiellonian University Medical College. Her main research focuses on re
 fugee health\, with focus on biomarkers\, such as cortisol and telomere l
 ength. She is also a research assistant in a project focusing on health s
 ystems barriers and facilitators for Ukrainian refugees in Poland.  \n\nR
 esearch projects: STRONG study Stress\, Trauma\, Resilience Of New Genera
 tions (PI: Grazyna Jasienska) EDuREF study Investigating the barriers and
  facilitators to emergency department use among refugees from Ukraine in 
 Poland (PI: Iwona Bielska)\n\nLunch is complimentary for registered atten
 dees.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260904T170513Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T170513Z
