CREATED:20260819T153700Z
DESCRIPTION:What songs carry memories of the people and places that have s
 haped us? In this interactive workshop\, participants will reflect on son
 gs connected to family\, home\, heritage\, or tradition and create a smal
 l collage-style memento that brings together music\, memory\, images\, an
 d words. Together\, we'll explore the ways songs can hold stories\, conne
 ct generations\, and become part of the everyday archives we carry with u
 s.\n\nLed by Duke music professor Dr. Sophia Enriquez\, part of "Forum @ 
 the Library"  - a monthly series featuring Duke faculty sharing their wor
 k in an interactive format\, hosted by the Durham County Library (DCL) in
  partnership with the Forum for Scholars and Publics at the Franklin Huma
 nities Institute.\n\nFree and open to the public.\n\nThis program will be
  held in the Main Children's Programming Room at the Durham County Librar
 y Main Library. While accompanied children are welcome\, we especially en
 courage adults and older teens to join us for this memory-focused worksho
 p.\n\nRegistration required at the DCL event page
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260819T165427Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260908T180000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T165427Z
