CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a0290b4-860465b2-0186-32feb568-0000477d:Spaulding\
 , Amy
CREATED:20260825T205439Z
DESCRIPTION:The Thomas Lord Department of Mechanical Engineering and Mater
 ial Science welcomes Kristina Johnson to present the MEMS Distinguished S
 eminar\, "The Intentional Entrepreneur" on Wed. September 9\, 2026. \n\nA
 BSTRACT: Entrepreneurship is not confined to startups\; it is a disciplin
 ed way of identifying consequential problems\, mobilizing people and reso
 urces\, and turning promising ideas into lasting impact. This talk draws 
 on lessons learned across academia\, government\, industry\, and venture 
 capital. At Duke University\, I co-founded Southeast TechInventures with 
 Karen LeVert to help faculty and students secure nondilutive SBIR and STT
 R funding\, supporting dozens of companies and several successful exits. 
 At the U.S. Department of Energy\, I helped launch ARPA-E\, the Technolog
 y Commercialization Office\, and the SBIR Xcelerator\, while advancing th
 e STEP energy strategy. I later co-founded Cube Hydro Partners\, a clean-
 energy platform sold to Ontario Power Generation for $1.12 billion.\nThat
  same entrepreneurial approach informed the creation of a systemwide entr
 epreneurship certificate for more than one million SUNY students\, the Pr
 esident's Buckeye Accelerator at The Ohio State University\, and now Cata
 lyzer Ventures\, a deep-tech firm investing in the energy transition\, th
 e built environment\, and industrial systems. Through these experiences\,
  The Intentional Entrepreneur offers candid\, tough-love lessons about ch
 oosing problems that matter\, building the right team\, navigating resist
 ance\, aligning capital with purpose\, and knowing when to persist\, pivo
 t\, or let go-including what I wish I had known at the outset\, but am gr
 ateful to have learned along the way.\n\nBIO:DR. JOHNSON has a distinguis
 hed record of achievement in higher education\, government\, and private 
 industry\, serving as President of The Ohio State University and Chancell
 or of the State University of New York (SUNY). Before joining SUNY\, Dr. 
 Johnson was founding CEO of Cube Hydro Partners\, LLC\,  a clean-energy i
 nfrastructure company focused on building\, upgrading\, and operating hyd
 ropower plants in North America.  \nPrior to Cube Hydro\, Dr. Johnson was
  appointed by President Obama and unanimously confirmed by the Senate as 
 Under Secretary of Energy at the U.S. Department of Energy. Dr. Johnson w
 as senior vice-president and provost at Johns Hopkins University and dean
  of the Pratt School of Engineering at Duke University.
DURATION:PT1H
